An Irq's notification keeps the second word of the capability it was bound with, and does not name the Irq.
A revoke that clears it would leave the Irq armed and its line unmasked;
an Irq's notification names its Irq.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: irq's notification does not name its irq
Witness: fuzz bind-restarts

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -733,7 +733,6 @@ static int op_irq_line(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *cap,
         struct irq *irq = pool_alloc(pool, CAP_IRQ, obj_type_size(CAP_IRQ, 0));
         /* It hangs below the capability it was bound with, so a revoke above that disarms the Irq. */
         irq->ntfn = nc;
-        irq->ntfn.b = held_word(v2p(irq), nc.b);
         cap_attach(slot_node(t, arg[2]), &irq->ntfn);
         irq->line = first;
         /* A period counts from the last deadline, and a line that never fired from its bind. */
